WEBVTT

00:06:58.633 --> 00:07:01.196
which is kind of the right mix,
if you ask me.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.221
(Laughter)

00:07:02.245 --> 00:07:04.092
But ... right?

00:07:04.116 --> 00:07:05.279
TZ: I agree.

00:07:05.303 --> 00:07:07.553
SB: But a Stentor is only a single cell.

00:07:07.577 --> 00:07:10.268
And it's able to sense
and react to its environment.

00:07:10.292 --> 00:07:13.188
You see, it will swim forward
when it's happy;

00:07:13.212 --> 00:07:16.276
it will swim backward when it's trying
to get away from something

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.322
like, you know, a toxic chemical.

00:07:18.713 --> 00:07:21.609
With our friends in the Center
for Cellular Construction

00:07:21.633 --> 00:07:24.069
and the help of the National
Science Foundation,

00:07:24.093 --> 00:07:28.641
we are using Stentor to sense the presence
of contamination in food and water,

00:07:28.665 --> 00:07:30.355
which I think is really cool.